THOUGHT: The NullAway error is because setSprite accepts a @Nullable Sprite and immediately dereferences it. I should allow null sprites without crashing by guarding the dereferences and setting min sizes to 0 when sprite is null. I’ll update the method accordingly and then run the NullAway build to confirm the error count decreases by one and no new errors are introduced.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/libgdx && sed -i '83,87c\  public void setSprite(@Nullable Sprite sprite) {
    this.sprite = sprite;
    if (sprite != null) {
      setMinWidth(sprite.getWidth());
      setMinHeight(sprite.getHeight());
    } else {
      setMinWidth(0);
      setMinHeight(0);
    }
  }' gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/scenes/scene2d/utils/SpriteDrawable.java && ./gradlew gdx:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1
```

